# Frontend Angular

Apply when editing frontend Angular files. Prefer existing patterns in `frontend/` over inventing new structure or state/networking stacks.

## Structure

```text
frontend/src/app/
├── core/                 # singleton services, guards, interceptors
├── shared/               # shared components, pipes, directives
├── features/<feature>/
│   ├── components/
│   ├── pages/            # or containers / routed components
│   ├── services/
│   ├── models/
│   └── <feature>.routes.ts
├── app.routes.ts
└── app.config.ts         # or app.module.ts if NgModules are used
```

Adapt to standalone vs NgModule layout if one is already established.

## Layering

- Components/templates: presentation and user interaction only.
- Routed pages/containers: compose child components; coordinate feature UI state.
- Services: HTTP (`HttpClient`), API mapping, and shared feature logic.
- Guards/interceptors: auth, cross-cutting request/response behavior.
- Models: TypeScript interfaces/types for API and view models.

## Conventions

- Keep API calls in injectable services; do not call `HttpClient` from templates or presentational components.
- Prefer reactive patterns already used in the app (`async` pipe, signals, or RxJS)—do not mix in a new approach without justification.
- Reuse `shared/` and existing feature components before creating new ones.
- Avoid fat components; move non-UI logic into services.
- Keep business rules that must be trusted on the server.
- Handle loading, success, empty, and error states where relevant.
- Prefer strongly typed models; avoid `any`.
- Follow existing styling approach (component SCSS, shared styles); do not invent a new CSS system.

## Example

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — component performs HTTP directly
@Component({ /* ... */ })
export class UserCardComponent implements OnInit {
  user?: User;
  constructor(private http: HttpClient) {}
  ngOnInit() {
    this.http.get<User>('/api/user').subscribe(u => (this.user = u));
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD — service owns HTTP; component renders
@Component({ /* ... */ })
export class UserCardComponent {
  user = input.required<User>();
}
```
